able4 td:nth-child(3) { width: 310px; }\n    .caption {\n      width: 900px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n      font-style: italic;\n      font-size: 30px;\n    }\n    h2 {\n      margin: 43px 0 15px;\n      font-size: 38px;\n      line-height: 1.2;\n    }\n    h3 {\n      margin: 39px 0 28px;\n      font-size: 38px;\n      line-height: 1.2;\n    }\n    .table5 {\n      width: 616px;\n      margin: 24px auto 0;\n    }\n    .table5 td:nth-child(1) { width: 116px; }\n    .table5 td:nth-child(2) { width: 323px; }\n    .table5 td:nth-child(3) { width: 177px; }\n    .table5-caption { width: 616px; }\n    .references-title {\n      margin-top: 55px;\n      font-size: 43px;\n    }\n    .normative-title {\n      margin-top: 34px;\n      margin-bottom: 27px;\n      font-size: 38px;\n    }\n    .references {\n      margin-left: 53px;\n      font-size: 29px;\n      line-height: 1.28;\n    }\n    .reference {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 168px 1fr;\n      column-gap: 0;\n      margin: 0 0 26px;\n    }\n    .reference-key {\n      font-weight: bold;\n    }\n    .running-footer {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 28px;\n      right: 28px;\n      bottom: 92px;\n      padding-top: 24px;\n      border-top: 2px solid #cfcfcf;\n      font-size: 28px;\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 1400px) {\n      .page {\n        width: 100%;\n        min-height: 100vh;\n        padding-left: 9.4%;\n        padding-right: 9.4%;\n      }\n      .content { margin-left: 2%; margin-right: 2%; }\n      .table4, .caption { max-width: 900px; width: 76%; }\n      .table5, .table5-caption { max-width: 616px; width: 58%; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"page\">\n    <header class=\"running-header\">\n      <div>RFC 9010</div>\n      <div>RPL-Unaware Leaves</div>\n      <div>April 2021</div>\n    </header>\n\n    <section class=\"content\">\n      <ul class=\"bullet-list\">\n        <li>The initial allocation is as indicated in <a href=\"#\">Table 4</a>:</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <table class=\"table4\">\n        <tr>\n          <td>Value</td>\n          <td>Meaning</td>\n          <td>Reference</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>0</td>\n          <td>Success / Unqualified acceptance</td>\n          <td>RFC 6550 / RFC 9010</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>1..63</td>\n          <td>Unassigned</td>\n          <td></td>\n        </tr>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"caption\">Table 4: Acceptance Values of the RPL Status</div>\n\n      <h2>12.6.&nbsp;&nbsp; New Subregistry for RPL Rejection Status Values</h2>\n\n      <p>IANA has created a new subregistry for the RPL Rejection Status values for use in the RPL DAO-<br>ACK and DCO messages with the 'A' flag set to 0 and the 'U' flag set to 1, under the \"Routing<br>Protocol for Low Power and Lossy Networks (RPL)\" registry.</p>\n\n      <ul class=\"bullet-list\">\n        <li>Possible values are 6-bit unsigned integers (0..63).</li>\n        <li>The registration procedure is IETF Review [<a href=\"#\">RFC8126</a>].</li>\n        <li>The initial allocation is as indicated in <a href=\"#\">Table 5</a>:</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <table class=\"table5\">\n        <tr>\n          <td>Value</td>\n          <td>Meaning</td>\n          <td>Reference</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>0</td>\n          <td>Unqualified rejection</td>\n          <td>RFC 9010</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>1</td>\n          <td>No routing entry</td>\n          <td>RFC 9009</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>2..63</td>\n          <td>Unassigned</td>\n          <td></td>\n        </tr>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"caption table5-caption\">Table 5: Rejection Values of the RPL Status</div>\n\n      <h2 class=\"references-title\">13.&nbsp;&nbsp; References</h2>\n      <h3 class=\"normative-title\">13.1.&nbsp;&nbsp; Normative References</h3>\n\n      <section class=\"references\">\n        <div class=\"reference\">\n          <div class=\"reference-key\">[RFC2119]</div>\n          <div>Bradner, S., \"Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate Requirement Levels\", BCP 14,<br>RFC 2119, DOI 10.17487/RFC2119, March 1997, &lt;<a href=\"#\">https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/<br>rfc2119</a>&gt;.</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"reference\">\n          <div class=\"reference-key\">[RFC3810]</div>\n          <div>Vida, R., Ed. and L. Costa, Ed., \"Multicast Listener Discovery Version 2 (MLDv2)<br>for IPv6\", RFC 3810, DOI 10.17487/RFC3810, June 2004, &lt;<a href=\"#\">https://www.rfc-<br>editor.org/info/rfc3810</a>&gt;.</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"reference\">\n          <div class=\"reference-key\">[RFC4861]</div>\n          <div>Narten, T., Nordmark, E., Simpson, W., and H. Soliman, \"Neighbor Discovery for<br>IP version 6 (IPv6)\", RFC 4861, DOI 10.17487/RFC4861, September 2007, &lt;<a href=\"#\">https://<br>www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc4861</a>&gt;.</div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n    </section>\n\n    <footer class=\"running-footer\">\n      <div>Thubert &amp; Richardson</div>\n      <div>Standards Track</div>\n      <div>Page 32</div>\n    </footer>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>"
